rror code\nL60: 0x80320001—0x80320039\nL61:  | A Windows Filtering Platform (WFP) specific error. See cite6†WFP Error Codes for details.\nL62: \nL63: RPC_* error code\nL64: 0x80010001—0x80010122\nL65:  | Failure to communicate with the remote or local firewall engine.\nL66: ## Remarks\nL67: \nL68: After an application has completed adding or removing system objects, it may call the FwpmEngineClose0 function to close the open session to the filter engine.\nL69: \nL70: A filter engine session is also closed when a client process terminates.\nL71: \nL72: If this function is called with a transaction in progress, the transaction will be aborted.\nL73: \nL74: FwpmEngineClose0 is a specific implementation of FwpmEngineClose. See cite7†WFP Version-Independent Names and Targeting Specific Versions of Windows for more information.\nL75: ## Requirements\nL76: \nL77: Requirement  | Value\nL78: --- | ---\nL79: Minimum supported client  | Windows Vista [desktop apps only]\nL80: Minimum supported server  | Windows Server 2008 [desktop apps only]\nL81: Target Platform  | Windows\nL82: Header  | fwpmu.h\nL83: Library  | Fwpuclnt.lib\nL84: DLL  | Fwpuclnt.dll\nL85: \nL86: ## See also\nL87: \nL88: cite5†FwpmEngineOpen0 L89: \nL90: cite8†Kernel-Mode FwpmEngineClose0 L91: \nL92: * * *\nL93: ## Feedback\nL94: \nL95: Was this page helpful?\nL96: \nL97: Yes No No\nL98: \nL99: Need help with this topic?\nL100: \nL101: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\nL102: \nL103: Ask Learn Ask Learn\nL104: \nL105: Suggest a fix?\nL106: \nL107: * * *\nL108: \nL109: ## Additional resources\nL110: \nL111: * * *\nL112: \nL113:   * Last updated on 2024-02-22\nL114: \nL115: ### In this article\nL116: \nL117: Was this page helpful?\nL118: \nL119: Need help with this topic?\nL120: \nL121: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\nL122: \nL123: Ask Learn Ask Learn\nL124: \nL125: Suggest a fix?\n--------------------------------------