: \nL51: Type: HANDLE\nL52: \nL53: Handle of a filter enumeration created by a call to cite5†FwpmFilterCreateEnumHandle0 .\nL54: ## Return value\nL55: \nL56: Type: DWORD\nL57: \nL58: Return code/value  | Description\nL59: --- | ---\nL60: \nL61: ERROR_SUCCESS\nL62: 0\nL63:  | The enumerator was successfully deleted.\nL64: \nL65: FWP_E_* error code\nL66: 0x80320001—0x80320039\nL67:  | A Windows Filtering Platform (WFP) specific error. See cite7†WFP Error Codes for details.\nL68: \nL69: RPC_* error code\nL70: 0x80010001—0x80010122\nL71:  | Failure to communicate with the remote or local firewall engine.\nL72: ## Remarks\nL73: \nL74: FwpmFilterDestroyEnumHandle0 is a specific implementation of FwpmFilterDestroyEnumHandle. See cite8†WFP Version-Independent Names and Targeting Specific Versions of Windows for more information.\nL75: \nL76: ## Requirements\nL77: \nL78: Requirement  | Value\nL79: --- | ---\nL80: Minimum supported client  | Windows Vista [desktop apps only]\nL81: Minimum supported server  | Windows Server 2008 [desktop apps only]\nL82: Target Platform  | Windows\nL83: Header  | fwpmu.h\nL84: Library  | Fwpuclnt.lib\nL85: DLL  | Fwpuclnt.dll\nL86: ## See also\nL87: \nL88: cite5†FwpmFilterCreateEnumHandle0 L89: \nL90: * * *\nL91: \nL92: ## Feedback\nL93: \nL94: Was this page helpful?\nL95: \nL96: Yes No No\nL97: \nL98: Need help with this topic?\nL99: \nL100: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\nL101: \nL102: Ask Learn Ask Learn\nL103: \nL104: Suggest a fix?\nL105: \nL106: * * *\nL107: \nL108: ## Additional resources\nL109: \nL110: * * *\nL111: \nL112:   * Last updated on 2024-02-22\nL113: \nL114: ### In this article\nL115: \nL116: Was this page helpful?\nL117: \nL118: Need help with this topic?\nL119: \nL120: Want to try using Ask Learn to clarify or guide you through this topic?\nL121: \nL122: Ask Learn Ask Learn\nL123: \nL124: Suggest a fix?\n--------------------------------------------------------------------